Subject: [PATCH] Regenerate scanners for the PHP 8.3.35 OOM candidate

Status: Candidate for private validation; not confirmed final upstream.
Embargoed: Keep this patch in private repositories until disclosure.

Companion to php-8.3.35-oom-candidate.patch, pinned to upstream revision
d59a20c8f9dcd3a7ecf2fb815d996c4e00c49348.

Generated locally with re2c 4.0.2, matching the PHP 8.3.35 release tarball,
using ext/standard/Makefile.frag and ext/json/Makefile.frag:

  re2c --no-generation-date -b -o ext/standard/var_unserializer.c ext/standard/var_unserializer.re
  re2c --no-generation-date -b -o ext/standard/url_scanner_ex.c ext/standard/url_scanner_ex.re
  re2c --no-generation-date -bci -t ext/json/php_json_scanner_defs.h -o ext/json/json_scanner.c ext/json/json_scanner.re

The generated C changes avoid requiring re2c in the Azure Linux build.
The JSON companion header is regenerated but unchanged.

